{{!--
    ember-ui's base cell renders {{or @value "-"}}, and zero is falsy — so a
    warehouse holding no stock, or an order with no line items, read as "unknown"
    rather than as none. For a count that is exactly the wrong way round.

    Long-form comment deliberately: a {{! }} comment ends at its first }}, and
    this one quotes a helper, so the short form spilled the rest into the cell.
--}}
<div class="relative" aria-label={{this.display}}>
    <span class={{@column.cellClassNames}}>{{this.display}}</span>
</div>